---
/*
 * The square brand mark: Hill 1, the site's two hills. A copper near hill
 * stands in front of a gray-green far hill, centered on the 64 grid. Both are
 * solid and take --mark-far / --mark-near, so the mark follows the theme.
 * Transparent background, per docs/BRAND.md §3. It lives behind this one seam so replacing it stays cheap.
 *
 * The same geometry is duplicated by necessity in `public/brand-mark.svg`
 * (the standalone shareable file) and `public/favicon.svg` (cropped tighter,
 * with a solid far hill for light tabs) — an .astro component cannot be served
 * as a raw asset. Change one, change all three.
 *
 * Plain inline SVG only (BRAND.md §4): the mark is expected to flow into the
 * Electron app, and that port should be a copy, not a rewrite.
 *
 * Sized in em so the parent's font-size scales it; decorative wherever the
 * product name is written next to it, hence aria-hidden.
 */
---

<svg
  class="brand-mark"
  viewBox="0 0 64 64"
  width="1em"
  height="1em"
  aria-hidden="true"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <path d="M4 49V35L18 23L26 29L38 15L60 33V49Z" fill="var(--mark-far, #5a6661)"></path>
  <path d="M4 49V41L18 31L26 37L34 31L46 23L60 39V49Z" fill="var(--mark-near, #cca250)"></path>
</svg>

<style>
  .brand-mark {
    display: block;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
</style>
